            <ArticleTitle>Gabapentin-induced coma in a patient with renal failure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>168-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 60-year-old woman who became comatose after a single dose of gabapentin for right-sided sciatalgia. The patient was improved by hemodialysis. Gabapentin toxicity should be considered when mental status changes develop in patients with renal failure after even a single dose.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
